  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Direct absolute F measurements for baclofen (73–86% in humans, 69% in dogs) and levodopa (63.6–86.4% across fasted/fed IR/CR formulations) show that zwitterionic amino-acid-like drugs can exceed F=20% despite high polarity and ionization.",
      "card_ids": ["C02", "C15", "C21", "C26", "C29", "C31", "C33"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records demonstrate meaningful systemic absorption of beta-lactams after oral dosing: ampicillin Cmax 9.53 µg/mL after 500 mg sultamicillin, amoxicillin Cmax 11.4 µg/mL after 200 mg in dogs, cefpodoxime Cmax 1.32 mg/L after 100 mg, and M01 Cmax 2.01–6.10 µg/mL over 50–400 mg.",
      "card_ids": ["C40", "C46", "C44", "C36", "C37"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The query is an alpha-amino-p-hydroxyphenylglycyl cephalosporin (cefatrizine), structurally analogous to the orally absorbed beta-lactams in C40/C44/C46; no affirmative threshold-relevant evidence supports F<20%, and the only negative signal (C25) is an indirect rat Cmax inference about baclofen metabolites.",
      "card_ids": ["C40", "C44", "C46", "C25"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": [
        "C36", "C37", "C38", "C39", "C40", "C41", "C42",
        "C43", "C44", "C45", "C46", "C47"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for cefatrizine is present in the supplied cards.",
    "L3 records report Cmax only, without matched IV AUC, so they do not quantify absolute F.",
    "PepT1-mediated transport and gastrointestinal stability of the query are not directly measured.",
    "Some L3 records involve prodrugs (sultamicillin, cefpodoxime proxetil) or dogs, limiting quantitative transfer.",
    "Species, formulation, and prandial differences prevent a numeric F estimate."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high and is strengthened: L3 adds oral Cmax evidence for beta-lactams (ampicillin, amoxicillin, cefpodoxime, M01) showing meaningful systemic exposure after oral dosing, consistent with prior direct F values for amino-acid-like drugs. The query cefatrizine shares the alpha-amino-p-hydroxyphenylglycyl cephem scaffold with these orally absorbed beta-lactams. Cmax alone is not F, and no direct query F is available, so confidence stays moderate."
}

